# I-BB Barrier Rubric

## 1. NASA-TLX-style structure (principle only — not NASA-TLX items or validation)

| NASA-TLX | I-BB Barrier Rubric |
|---|---|
| Specifies a target task | Specifies a target behaviour |
| Measures multiple workload dimensions | Measures three barrier dimensions |
| Gives each dimension a separate rating | Gives DFE, LKA, POI separate scores |
| Produces a multidimensional profile | Produces a three-barrier profile |
| Applied across different tasks | Applied across behavioural domains |

Unlike weighted NASA-TLX, this inventory does **not**: conduct pairwise importance weighting; produce one overall barrier score; average DFE/LKA/POI together; or multiply two scores to create a configuration. It reports three independent scores.

## 2. Instructions
"This behaviour" refers to: **[insert target behaviour, situation and context]**

| Domain | Referent |
|---|---|
| Online commenting | Writing a constructive comment when responding to content or another person online |
| Sedentary behaviour | Interrupting a prolonged period of sitting by engaging in brief physical activity |
| PET recycling | Removing the label from a PET bottle before placing the bottle in a recycling bin when label removal is required |

## 3. Response scale
1=Strongly disagree · 2=Disagree · 3=Neither agree nor disagree · 4=Agree · 5=Strongly agree. All items keyed consistently: higher response = stronger barrier. No reverse-scored items.

---

## 4. DFE — Distance from Effect
*Perceived separation between a behaviour and its consequences: distant, delayed, invisible, insignificant, or insufficiently salient at the point of execution.*

| Code | Item | Facet | Citation |
|---|---|---|---|
| DFE1 | The consequences of this behaviour are farther in time and place from the moment I perform it. | Consequence distance | [12], [17], [19], [29] |
| DFE2 | The effects of this behaviour are difficult to see immediately. | Immediate visibility | [6], [28] |
| DFE3 | Performing this behaviour once seems unlikely to make a noticeable difference. | Perceived individual impact | [10], [14], [21], [25], [26] |
| DFE4 | It is difficult to connect this behaviour with its eventual consequences. | Action–outcome connection | [7], [11], [22], [30] |
| DFE5 | The consequences of this behaviour rarely come to mind when I decide how to act. | Consequence salience at execution | [40], [6], [37] |

## 5. LKA — Lack of Knowledge/Awareness
*Insufficient procedural, situational, consequence-related, or rule-related understanding needed to recognise and perform the behaviour appropriately.*

| Code | Item | Facet | Citation |
|---|---|---|---|
| LKA1 | I am uncertain about how to perform this behaviour correctly. | Procedural knowledge | [2], [24], [26], [32] |
| LKA2 | I am uncertain about what actions this behaviour requires. | Requirement awareness | [1], [13], [16], [25], [39] |
| LKA3 | I am uncertain about the situations in which this behaviour should be performed. | Situational recognition | [20], [23], [26] |
| LKA4 | I lack information about the consequences of performing or not performing this behaviour. | Consequence knowledge | [5], [7] |
| LKA5 | The information or guidance available about this behaviour is difficult to understand. | Guidance comprehension | [3], [15], [21], [23], [38] |

## 6. POI — Perception of Inconvenience
*The extent to which the behaviour is perceived as effortful, time-consuming, disruptive, troublesome, or difficult in the relevant context.*

| Code | Item | Facet | Citation |
|---|---|---|---|
| POI1 | Performing this behaviour requires too much effort. | Perceived effort | [22], [26], [28], [30], [32], [33], [37], [39] |
| POI2 | Performing this behaviour is inconvenient within my normal routine. | Routine disruption | [9], [18], [23], [34] |
| POI3 | Performing this behaviour takes more time than I would prefer. | Perceived time cost | [16], [30] |
| POI4 | The actions required to perform this behaviour are troublesome. | Procedural burden | [23], [26], [33], [36] |
| POI5 | It is difficult to perform this behaviour in the situations where it is needed. | Situational inconvenience | [10], [27], [30], [31], [32], [34], [37] |

